  "body": "VIEW BY APPOINTMENT ( James Dixon 0210360747/ Wenli Hu 02102863780) \r\nHarcourts property files: https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/PVR2\r\n\r\nSet within established landscaped grounds and enjoying pleasant sea views, this elevated freehold residence offers a relaxed and considered approach to contemporary coastal living.\r\n\r\nDesigned with generous proportions and an emphasis on light, space and connection, the home provides an inviting environment for family life, quiet moments and easy entertaining.\r\n\r\nThe main living spaces flow naturally to expansive balconies, creating a wonderful sense of connection between indoors and out. There is plenty of room for everyone to find their own space, while the flexible layout makes coming together equally effortless.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of the home is a beautifully appointed kitchen, featuring natural marble benchtops and quality Gaggenau appliances. A discreet second kitchenette adds further convenience when entertaining, allowing the main kitchen to remain the social heart of the home.\r\n\r\nThe five bedrooms are generously proportioned, with three enjoying their own en-suites and walk-in wardrobes. The master suite feels particularly peaceful, with a beautifully finished en-suite complete with a bathtub and separate shower.\r\n\r\nA dedicated study on the upper level provides a quiet place to work or study, while the separate laundry has been thoughtfully designed for everyday family life.\r\n\r\nThroughout the home, natural materials and considered finishes create a sense of understated quality. Cedar and rendered brick give the exterior a contemporary coastal character, while inside, carefully selected tiles and brushed-nickel Grohe fittings add a refined touch.\r\n\r\nPracticality has been thoughtfully considered too, with a four-car garage, four additional on-site parking spaces and secure gated entry. CCTV provides added peace of mind.\r\n\r\nBeyond the home, Long Bay offers an enviable coastal lifestyle. Long Bay Beach and Regional Park are close by, along with local shops, restaurants and everyday amenities. Families will also appreciate the zoning for Long Bay Primary, Northcross Intermediate and Long Bay College.\r\n\r\nAbove all, this is a home with room to live - a place where family, friends and everyday moments can be enjoyed in a beautiful coastal setting.\r\n\r\nPlease feel free to park on  site during the viewing.",
